components.responsibility:
**TestEveryScreenIsDesigned** uses newHarness(t, false) on its real listener and headless.Open (CHROME_BIN only). Sessions come from mint/mintUser and are set with Network.setCookie. AvatarURLs point at a same-origin 404, so Chrome never leaves the machine.

Seed, through the existing helpers and routes:
- the owner, a reader with a 39-character login, and a second reader who is later blocked;
- one published and one draft report;
- a chain deeper than threadDepthCap, an owner comment (Author badge), a 300-character unbroken body, and a removed comment with a visible reply;
- a reader vote; reader feedback with an owner reply;
- a comment and feedback from the second reader, who is then blocked.

States:
- anonymous: /, /reports/<slug>, /reports, the branch page;
- reader: /, /reports/<slug>, /reports/<slug>#feedback-sent, /reports, the branch page, GET /admin (the forbidden page);
- owner: /reports/<slug>, /admin, /admin after a refused upload, /admin/reports/<slug>, /admin/blocked;
- a second, empty harness as the owner: /, /reports, /admin/blocked.

The refused upload is a real Chrome form POST: Eval fills title and an invalid slug, sets noValidate and calls submit(), then polls for p.error.

Passes: each state is navigated at 1280x900 and at 375x812 mobile. Per width, the scheme is set to light, then dark, with Emulation.setEmulatedMedia. Pages with details get a second pass with every details opened.

Each pass runs probe.js and asserts:
- (a) 0 <style> elements and 0 [style] attributes; document.styleSheets is exactly /static/site.css; the <script count is 1 on the found reader and branch pages and 0 elsewhere.
- (b) No visible a[href], button, non-hidden input, select, textarea, summary, th or td matches the bare.html element of the same tag and type in the same scheme on all of: color, background-color, border-top style/width/colour, border-radius, text-decoration-line, font-family, font-size, padding-top and padding-left. A file input is judged on ::file-selector-button.
- (c) documentElement.scrollWidth <= innerWidth.
- (d) Every text-bearing element is at least 4.5:1 against its nearest opaque ancestor background. Every filled or bordered control reaches at least 3:1 (the larger of fill and border against its parent). A non-rgb colour, or a background with 0<alpha<1, fails as unmeasurable.
- (e) html's background is opaque and differs between the two schemes. This also proves the live scheme switch took effect.
- (f) #feedback-sent has no client rects unless the fragment targets it. Each button.toggle, given hidden again by Eval, computes display none.
- (g) Role checks: the confirm buttons in .remove and .block and the Delete button compute the danger fill; the Upload, Post, Reply, Send and sign-in controls compute the accent fill.
- (h) Desktop Page.captureScreenshot of the owner's reader page and the three admin pages, in both schemes and with details open, has 0 pixels within 8 of #ff0000 or #00ff00 (headless.Count).

**TestReportFrameKeepsItsOwnCanvas.** The owner publishes three reports:
- A: no background and no color-scheme;
- B: an `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` html background of #204060;
- C: `:root { color-scheme: light dark }` and no background.

Under light and under dark, at 1280x1000, it captures /reports/<slug> and takes the mean of a 5x5 patch inside the frame's empty right edge, located from the frame's bounding rect. It captures /raw/<slug> opened alone at the same offset. The two patches must agree within ±8 per channel.

Sensitivity control: for A under dark, the patch outside the frame (the site's dark --bg) must differ from the inside patch by more than 8. This proves the test can see the site surface.

