cross_domain_transfer.rationale:
The slice has exactly that structure. The site must look designed under two viewing conditions, the report must look as it does standalone under both, and the one measured no-go was a substrate leak. Selected from it:
- the palette table with per-pair contrast checked statically (folded into TestStylesheetTokens);
- Canvas under the frame, with color-scheme never set on the frame;
- the embedded-equals-standalone oracle (TestReportFrameKeepsItsOwnCanvas).

stack_chosen.choice:
Site styling is one hand-written, same-origin stylesheet, internal/server/static/site.css:
- custom-property tokens with light-dark() for dark mode;
- no at-rules;
- no CSS preprocessor, framework or build step;
- the system-ui font stack and no webfont.

Every page's document shell comes from internal/layout's html/template partials.
